-- title:
--   Two generators suffice for the level-N modular function field
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, let $\ell$ be a natural number which is the characteristic of $K$ (so $\ell = 0$ is allowed), let $N$ be a nonzero natural number, and assume $\ell \nmid N$. Inside the field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ K$ of Laurent series over $K$, write $j(q)$ for the series `jqModC K`, namely $q^{-1}$ times the image under $K$-coefficient reduction of the power series `jNum`, and for a natural number $d$ write $\mathrm{qExpand}\ K\ d$ for the substitution $q \mapsto q^{d}$ on Laurent series. The theorem asserts the equality of two intermediate fields of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ K$ over $K$: the field `modularFunctionFieldC K N` obtained by adjoining to $K$ the two elements $j(q)$ and $\mathrm{qExpand}\ K\ N\,(j(q))$, and the field `modularFunctionFieldFullC K N` obtained by adjoining to $K$ the whole set `divisorExpansionsC K N` of all series $\mathrm{qExpand}\ K\ d\,(j(q))$ with $d$ a nonzero divisor of $N$. Thus every divisor-level expansion $j(q^{d})$, $d \mid N$, already lies in the field generated over $K$ by $j(q)$ and $j(q^{N})$.
--
--   This is the generation statement for the function field of the modular curve of level $N$ in the $q$-expansion model: the field is generated by $j$ and $j_N$ alone, not only by all intermediate $j(q^d)$. It is used throughout the project wherever a construction attached to one of the two descriptions of the level-$N$ function field has to be transported to the other, in particular for the special-fibre constructions at a characteristic $\ell$ prime to the level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_modularFunctionFieldC_eq_modularFunctionFieldFullC.lean

